    "abstract": "Parts figure for the aft fuselage frames and their feet in the bilge area, covering the cleat and shear tie standard, the renewal splice set used on four-engine aircraft and the grommet and fastener detail.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the frame, frame foot, cleat and shear tie items in the bilge area of the aft fuselage, together with the splice items used when a foot is renewed.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows a typical frame station looking forward; the frames between the working stations are identical apart from their web depth. Sheet 2 shows the splice detail used when a foot is cut back and renewed. Items 40 and 50 are the renewal splice items and are not fitted at build; they appear on an aircraft only after a frame foot renewal has been recorded, and they are not interchangeable with the build items they sit on. They could not be added at the end of the family without separating them from the frame details they belong with, so the grommet, bolt, nut and rivet items move from 40, 50, 60, 70 and 80 to 60, 70, 80, 90 and 100, and the tension bolt at the foot moves to 110. Orders raised against the earlier item numbers remain traceable through the part number. Grommet items are called out per systems penetration and the count varies by aircraft."
    },
